{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "JOB",
  "chapter": 6,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "JOB.6.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.6.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But Job answered and said,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.6.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.6.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Oh that my grief were thoroughly weighed, and my calamity laid in the balances together!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.6.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.6.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For now it would be heavier than the sand of the sea: therefore my words are swallowed up.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.6.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.6.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the arrows of the Almighty ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " within me, the poison of which drinketh up my spirit: the terrors of God set themselves in array against me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.6.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.6.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Doth the wild ass bray when he hath grass? or loweth the ox over his fodder?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.6.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.6.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Can that which is unsavory be eaten without salt? or is there ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "any",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " taste in the white of an egg?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.6.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.6.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The things ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " my soul refused to touch ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " as my sorrowful food.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.6.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.6.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Oh that I might have my request; and that God would grant ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "me",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the thing that I long for!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.6.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.6.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Even that it would please God to destroy me; that he would let loose his hand, and cut me off!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.6.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.6.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then should I yet have comfort; yes, I would harden myself in sorrow: let him not spare; for I have not concealed the words of the Holy One.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.6.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.6.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "What ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " my strength, that I should hope? and what ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " my end, that I should prolong my life?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.6.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.6.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " my strength the strength of stones? or ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " my flesh of brass?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.6.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.6.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not my help in me? and is wisdom driven quite from me?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.6.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.6.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "To him that is afflicted pity ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "should be shown",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " from his friend; but he forsaketh the fear of the Almighty.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.6.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.6.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My brethren have dealt deceitfully as a brook, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " as the stream of brooks they pass away;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.6.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.6.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Which are blackish by reason of the ice, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in which the snow is hid:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.6.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.6.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "In the time when they become warm, they vanish: when it is hot, they are consumed out of their place.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.6.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.6.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The paths of their way are turned aside; they go to nothing, and perish.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.6.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.6.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The troops of Tema looked, the companies of Sheba waited for them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.6.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.6.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They were confounded because they had hoped; they came thither, and were ashamed.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.6.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.6.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For now ye are nothing: ye see ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "my",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " casting down, and are afraid.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.6.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.6.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Did I say, Bring to me? or Give a reward for me of your substance?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.6.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.6.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Or, Deliver me from the enemy's hand? or, Redeem me from the hand of the mighty?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.6.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.6.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Teach me, and I will hold my tongue: and cause me to understand in what I have erred.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.6.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.6.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "How forcible are right words! but what doth your arguing reprove?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.6.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.6.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Do ye imagine to reprove words, and the speeches of one that is desperate, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "which are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " as wind?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.6.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.6.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Yes, ye overwhelm the fatherless, and ye dig ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "a pit",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " for your friend.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.6.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.6.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now therefore be content, look upon me; for ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " evident to you if I lie.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.6.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.6.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Return, I pray you, let it not be iniquity; yes, return again, my righteousness ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.6.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.6.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Is there iniquity in my tongue? cannot my taste discern perverse things?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
